---
title: Backport Lifecycle
config:
    layout: elk
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> ready_for_backport: from process incident-response (IC determines backport required)

    ready_for_backport --> cherry_picking: developer claims backport
    cherry_picking --> backport_pr_review: developer opens backport PR (to process pr-review)

    backport_pr_review --> backport_merged: from process pr-review (backport PR merged to release branch)

    backport_merged --> patch_releasing: patch release triggered (to process release, IC bypass of release gate)
    patch_releasing --> backported: from process release (patch deployed to production)

    backported --> [*]: terminal (shipped)

    note right of ready_for_backport
        Entry: IC determines that main has diverged from the production release tag, so the hotfix on main is not sufficient. A backport is scoped to the affected older release branch.
    end note

    note right of cherry_picking
        Working. Developer cherry-picks the hotfix commit(s) onto the release branch, resolves conflicts, and opens a backport PR.
    end note

    note right of backport_pr_review
        Resting. The backport PR runs through the pr-lifecycle diagram like any other PR — reviewer feedback, QA, merge conflicts all happen there without advancing this diagram's state. The backport only advances to backport_merged when the PR is merged.
    end note

    note right of backport_merged
        Resting. Backport is on the release branch but not yet deployed. Hand off to release lifecycle as a patch release (v{major}.{minor}.{patch+1}).
    end note

    note right of patch_releasing
        Resting. Release lifecycle handles the patch train. Because a backport is always tied to an active incident mitigation, the IC authorizes bypass of the release gate (same authority as the main-branch hotfix).
    end note

    note right of backported
        Terminal (shipped). Patch release is live on the older version. If multiple release branches need backports, each is its own backport lifecycle instance.
    end note
